INT. SKATE PARK CONCESSION SHACK - DUSK

Hot dog roller. Neon "OPEN" buzzing. Outside, wheels rattle on concrete.

ZEKE ADEBAYO, 16, hoodie, sits on an upturned milk crate. His friend MILO FERRANTI-SATO, 16, leans on the counter. A radio on the shelf murmurs.

MILO
So she said yes.

ZEKE
She said maybe.

MILO
Maybe is yes with a coat on.

ZEKE
Maybe is "I'll text you" and then never.

MILO
She wrote it on your hand.

ZEKE
In pencil. It's smudged.

MILO
Dude. It's still in the shape of a number.

ZEKE
It's in the shape of a seven.

MILO
Then she's lucky. Seven's lucky.

ZEKE
Is that supposed to help?

MILO
No. I just wanted to say it.

JUNE (O.S.)
(outside, shrill)
Somebody get a towel! Now!

Both boys look up. Zeke slides off the crate.

ZEKE
That's her.

MILO
That's a fight.

Outside, shouting. A board clatters. Zeke and Milo bolt for the door and collide in the frame, jam, untangle, and spill out onto the concrete.

EXT. SKATE PARK - CONTINUOUS

A knot of kids around the bowl. At the centre, JUNE, 16, nose bleeding, faces a bigger boy. The crowd scatters as sirens approach, boards under arms.

Zeke stops. Milo almost runs into him.

ZEKE
There she is.

JUNE
(spotting him, wiping her nose)
Zeke! You came!

ZEKE
I came.

She grins through the blood and holds up her hand. A phone number, smudged across the palm. Fresh ink.

JUNE
Got it written again. Permanent marker.

Zeke laughs, huge and helpless, as the blue lights wash over them all.
